    <briefdescription>
<para>Persistent, append-only log of update operations. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Entries are written as a JSON array to a single log file. The file is read on construction and appended on every <ref refid="classthemis_1_1updates_1_1_update_history_logger_1ae5e504df12be3bbe97c5d4f45cd30325" kindref="member">record</ref> call. The class is intentionally lightweight and does not depend on RocksDB or any heavy storage layer.</para>
<para><heading level="3">Thread Safety</heading>
</para>
<para>All public methods are protected by an internal mutex and are safe to call from multiple threads.</para>
<para><heading level="3">Usage</heading>
</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classthemis_1_1updates_1_1_update_history_logger_1ae06805b3fb731cd5ab9f639097296807" kindref="member">UpdateHistoryLogger</ref><sp/>logger(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;/var/lib/themisdb/update_history.json&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">UpdateHistoryEntry<sp/>e;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">e.who<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>=<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;admin&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">e.from_version<sp/>=<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;1.4.0&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">e.to_version<sp/><sp/><sp/>=<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;1.5.0&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">e.event_type<sp/><sp/><sp/>=<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;update&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">e.success<sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>=<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">true</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">e.timestamp_ms<sp/>=<sp/>std::chrono::duration_cast&lt;std::chrono::milliseconds&gt;(</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>std::chrono::system_clock::now().time_since_epoch()).count();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">logger.record(e);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>history<sp/>=<sp/>logger.getHistory(10);<sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>last<sp/>10<sp/>entries</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
